# 3 Carat Lab Grown Marquise Diamond ({{year}}): 4 Ways to Spot Real Value

![Three 3 carat lab grown marquise cut diamonds held in jeweler tweezers against a white backdrop with text overlay reading 3 Carat Lab Marquise Diamond 4 Ways to Spot Real Value as the DiamondCritics featured image](/images/3-carat-lab-marquise-diamond.jpg "3 Carat Lab Marquise Diamond 4 Ways to Spot Real Value")

## TL;DR — 3 Carat Lab Marquise in One Scroll

**A 3 carat lab grown marquise diamond starts at $3,819 in current certified inventory.** Natural D-VVS1 equivalent costs $30,000+. That is 4.6x more for chemically identical carbon.

**The 4 ways to spot real value at 3ct — before product picks:**

1. **Skip D-VVS1, buy D-VVS2.** IGI D-VVS2 costs $4,756 vs D-VVS1 at $6,515. Save $1,759 for a colour difference invisible at 3ct.
2. **Demand Excellent or Ideal cut.** Very Good cut at 3ct hides bow-tie shadows. Three stones in current inventory list D-VS1 Very Good — skip them.
3. **Use the sub-3ct arbitrage.** 2.82ct E-VS1 Ideal at $3,289 vs 3.00ct E-VS1 at $3,819. Save $530, keep near-3ct weight.
4. **Choose IGI over GIA for lab.** GIA D-VVS1 costs $8,257 vs IGI $6,515. That $1,742 premium is the Cert Tax on a lab stone.

**The 3 key price points:**
- **Entry — IGI 3ct E-VS1 Ideal at $3,819:** Cheapest certified 3.00ct lab marquise in inventory. Eye-clean, brilliant white.
- **Value — IGI 3ct D-VVS2 Excellent at $4,756:** Top colour + VVS2 cert. $1,759 less than D-VVS1.
- **Premium — IGI 3ct D-VVS1 Very Good at $6,515:** Max IGI grade. Watch the bow-tie in 360° video (Very Good cut).

**Sub-3ct arbitrage:** IGI 2.82ct E-VS1 Ideal at $3,289 — $530 less than 3.00ct entry, 0.18ct lighter.

→ Entry pick: **[IGI 3ct E-VS1 Ideal at $3,819](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30343375?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Value pick: **[IGI 3ct D-VVS2 Excellent at $4,756](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30101251?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Arbitrage pick: **[IGI 2.82ct E-VS1 Ideal at $3,289](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30163288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

**Priority:** The D-VVS2 at $4,756 is the rational ceiling at 3ct. D-VVS1 at $6,515 adds $1,759 for a grade difference only a loupe reveals. See the full [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) for shape fundamentals.

## Expert Summary

Certified 3ct lab grown marquise inventory runs from **$2,646** (sub-3ct arbitrage) to **$11,108** (IGI D-IF Ideal). True 3.00ct stones range from $3,819 (IGI E-VS1 entry) to $8,257 (GIA D-VVS1). Natural 3ct D-VVS1 marquise costs $30,000+. The lab entry at $3,819 saves 75% vs a natural G-VS2 equivalent.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a diamond expert. At 3ct, the market hides value behind certification names and cut labels. Two stones can both say "D-VVS2" — one costs $4,756 with Excellent cut, one costs $5,765 with Ideal cut. The $1,009 gap is not better quality. It is better marketing. The 4 ways in this guide cut through that. Full profile at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every marquise topic.

This guide covers The 3ct Price Cliff, The Sub-3ct Arbitrage, and The Cert Tax. It includes grade-by-grade pricing and the complete $2,646–$11,108 inventory table. All prices verified against live certified market data.

