**Verdict:** D-VVS2 Excellent at $4,756 is the value ceiling. Every stone above it adds cost without adding visible quality. D-VVS1 adds a clarity tier invisible to the eye and comes with Very Good cut risk at 3ct. D-IF adds $6,352 for a certificate grade only. The setting investment matters far more than any grade above D-VVS2 at this size.

## Setting Pairing for 3ct Lab Grown Marquise

A 3ct lab marquise measures approximately 17x8mm face-up. This is a statement stone. It is longer and wider than at 2ct. The tips are more exposed. Setting choice is not optional — it determines durability.

**Six-prong solitaire — non-negotiable for safety.** At 17mm length, the pointed tips carry real exposure risk. Prongs at each tip and two on each side give full protection. A six-prong solitaire from $1,355 in white gold keeps the total ring under $5,200 with the D-VVS2 entry stone. See our [marquise solitaire engagement ring guide](/marquise-solitaire-engagement-ring).

**Bezel for maximum protection.** A full bezel completely wraps both tips. At 3ct, bezel is the safest daily-wear option for an active lifestyle. Total ring with E-VS1 entry: under $5,100. Trade-off: the metal lip slightly reduces side brilliance. See our [marquise bezel engagement ring guide](/marquise-bezel-engagement-ring).

**Pavé for visual impact.** A 3ct marquise at centre with pavé shoulders is one of the largest visual footprints in the engagement ring market. The 17mm stone fills the finger. Total ring with D-VVS2: under $6,700.

**Metal pairing:** D and E colour lab stones look best in platinum or white gold. Cool metal amplifies the colourless appearance. At 3ct, platinum tip prongs are worth considering — white gold requires replating, and at this stone length, tip wear shows faster. See our [platinum marquise engagement ring guide](/platinum-marquise-engagement-ring) and [white gold marquise engagement ring guide](/white-gold-marquise-engagement-ring).

